"""
Tutorial 2 — Linearization.

Linearizes the open-loop F16 plant about the trim operating point, from the four control
inputs with aerodynamic effect (uT, uEl, uAil, uRud — the leading-edge flap is inert in
this plant) to the 12 measured outputs (yn..yR). It reuses the instrumented design model
`LQGDemo` (03_lqg_continuous.dyad) and opens the feedback loop at the measurement
outputs, so the plant keeps its trim command inputs while the controller feedback is
severed — the result is the bare plant P, not the closed loop. Analysis-point names are
scalar, one per channel (see the note in 03).

Output: poles, zeros, and Bode/step responses of the linearized plant.
"""
analysis TutorialLinearize
  extends DyadControlSystems.LinearAnalysis(inputs = ["uT", "uEl", "uAil", "uRud"], outputs = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"], loop_openings = ["yn", "ye", "yalt", "yphi", "ypitch", "ypsi", "yvt", "yalpha", "ybeta", "yP", "yQ", "yR"])
  model = LQGDemo()
relations
end
